        "file": "ventures/sql-migration-lock-check/engine.mjs",
        "issue": "DDL inside a DO $$ ... $$ block was invisible: the body is a dollar-quoted string, so the masker blanked it and `DO $$ BEGIN IF NOT EXISTS (...) THEN CREATE INDEX idx ON users (email); END IF; END $$;` (the idiomatic conditional-DDL migration) came back verdict 'clean'. Same for ALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN / volatile defaults with no lock_timeout, and CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY inside DO (which PostgreSQL refuses). Fixed: expandDoBlocks splices the body's statements into the walk, at their own lines, inside the block's one transaction; 7 failing-first tests in engine.test.mjs.",
        "patched": true
